app/release/
*.log

# -------------------------
# graphify
# -------------------------
# The graph itself is tracked: graphify ships a merge driver for graph.json and a post-checkout hook, both of which assume it is under version control.
# The extraction cache stays out - it is large, machine-local, and rebuildable.
graphify-out/cache/*

# The generated graph viewer: 3 MB of HTML, rebuilt on every run and referenced by nothing - not CLAUDE.md, not AGENTS.md, not a workflow. Tracked, it
# made GitHub read the repo as an HTML project and added its 3 MB to history on every update. Rebuild it with `graphify cluster-only .` to look at it.
graphify-out/graph.html

# Dated snapshots graphify writes before it overwrites a curated graph. Useful
# locally for recovering hand-written community names; noise in history.
graphify-out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/

# Machine-local sidecars: absolute paths to this machine's Python and checkout.
# Wrong on every other machine, rewritten on each run.
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root
